  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "38137528",
      "title": "Adding a First Reducer & Store Setup",
      "lectureOrder": 688,
      "videoOrder": 633,
      "sourceHash": "e7c833bf0943e32edcff7c2d14f514a40d612112e4d11345770b1b426c3bea28",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 3.994,
          "en": "So we added NgRx,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.994,
          "end": 5.43,
          "en": "and therefore now it's of course time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.43,
          "end": 8.46,
          "en": "to make sure that we also have some data in that Store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.46,
          "end": 11.07,
          "en": "some data that can be used in our Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.07,
          "end": 14.31,
          "en": "For example, here in the counter-output-component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.31,
          "end": 16.92,
          "en": "I wanna read data from that Store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.92,
          "end": 19.89,
          "en": "I wanna get the current counter value from that Store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.89,
          "end": 22.47,
          "en": "so that I can then output it on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.47,
          "end": 24.87,
          "en": "with help of this component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.87,
          "end": 29.19,
          "en": "Now, to get data into the Store, we need a Reducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.19,
          "end": 33.42,
          "en": "Because ultimately in this NgRx architecture here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.42,
          "end": 38.1,
          "en": "Reducers are the things that change the data in the Store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.1,
          "end": 41.28,
          "en": "So if we just wanna set up some initial data for now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.28,
          "end": 43.5,
          "en": "we still need a Reducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.5,
          "end": 46.8,
          "en": "because it's that Reducer that sets up the initial value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.8,
          "end": 51.09,
          "en": "and then potentially changes it over time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.09,
          "end": 53.85,
          "en": "So to get some data into our Store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.85,
          "end": 58.23,
          "en": "or to also change that data later, we need a Reducer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.23,
          "end": 61.14,
          "en": "and that's therefore what we're going to start with now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.14,
          "end": 63.39,
          "en": "For that, in this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.39,
          "end": 67.08,
          "en": "here in my app folder I'll add a new folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.08,
          "end": 71.07,
          "en": "which I'll name Store or Counter Store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.07,
          "end": 72.27,
          "en": "This name is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.27,
          "end": 76.14,
          "en": "but this will be the folder where I wanna store some",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.14,
          "end": 79.17,
          "en": "NgRx specific files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.17,
          "end": 82.74,
          "en": "For example, the file that will define my Reducers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.74,
          "end": 86.85,
          "en": "And I will Store those files in a folder called Store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.85,
          "end": 91.443,
          "en": "because NgRx is all about having that global data Store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.31,
          "end": 94.71000000000001,
          "en": "Now, even though it's just one Store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.71000000000001,
          "end": 97.2,
          "en": "you could have different Reducer files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.2,
          "end": 99.57,
          "en": "for different parts of your application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.57,
          "end": 101.75999999999999,
          "en": "but you will see this later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.75999999999999,
          "end": 104.25,
          "en": "For the moment, it's this one Store folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.25,
          "end": 107.16,
          "en": "in this app folder, which I'm creating here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.16,
          "end": 108.6,
          "en": "And in that folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.6,
          "end": 113.6,
          "en": "I'll now add a Counter.Reducer.ts file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 113.78999999999999,
          "end": 117.96000000000001,
          "en": "And my goal now is to add the Reducer that is responsible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.96000000000001,
          "end": 120.69,
          "en": "for managing the data that belongs to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.69,
          "end": 124.623,
          "en": "this counterpart of this app in this file here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.73,
          "end": 129.15,
          "en": "For that, in the Counter.Reducer.ts file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 129.15,
          "end": 132.6,
          "en": "I'll start by creating a new constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 132.6,
          "end": 136.47,
          "en": "a new variable in the end that will never change though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 136.47,
          "end": 138.6,
          "en": "hence I'll make it a constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.6,
          "end": 141.143,
          "en": "which I will name counterReducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 142.53,
          "end": 143.79,
          "en": "Now the name is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.79,
          "end": 146.31,
          "en": "but this name here makes a lot of sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.31,
          "end": 148.74,
          "en": "because in the end it will be a Reducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 148.74,
          "end": 152.52,
          "en": "that is responsible for managing my counter data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.52,
          "end": 155.76,
          "en": "And such a Reducer can now be created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.76,
          "end": 157.563,
          "en": "with help of createReducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 158.64,
          "end": 161.647,
          "en": "And that is a function that can be imported from",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 161.647,
          "end": 164.733,
          "en": "@NgRx/Store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 166.11,
          "end": 170.22,
          "en": "So that's a function provided by this third party library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 170.22,
          "end": 174.03,
          "en": "that will create such a Reducer thing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 174.03,
          "end": 175.02,
          "en": "Now, under the hood,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 175.02,
          "end": 178.17000000000002,
          "en": "a Reducer, in the end, is just a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 178.17000000000002,
          "end": 181.2,
          "en": "that takes some data as input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.2,
          "end": 184.14,
          "en": "and spits out the updated State,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 184.14,
          "end": 187.38,
          "en": "the updated counter State in this case here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 187.38,
          "end": 190.95,
          "en": "So the updated data that should be Stored in that Store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 190.95,
          "end": 193.53,
          "en": "that's what a Reducer is under the hood,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 193.53,
          "end": 196.92000000000002,
          "en": "but we'll take a closer look under the hood of a Reducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 196.92000000000002,
          "end": 198.963,
          "en": "in the next lecture actually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 200.07,
          "end": 203.79,
          "en": "So here, we'll just create it with help of createReducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 203.79,
          "end": 206.43,
          "en": "And then this createReducer function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 206.43,
          "end": 208.53,
          "en": "needs at least one argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 208.53,
          "end": 211.59,
          "en": "And that one argument, which it needs at least,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 211.59,
          "end": 216.59,
          "en": "is the initialState of that piece of the global Store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 217.68,
          "end": 219.57,
          "en": "And for that, I'll add another constant here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 219.57,
          "end": 221.1,
          "en": "which I'll name initialState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 221.1,
          "end": 223.02,
          "en": "though this name also is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 223.02,
          "end": 225.54,
          "en": "It doesn't have to be initialState,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 225.54,
          "end": 227.34300000000002,
          "en": "but here I'll name it initialState.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 228.6,
          "end": 230.37,
          "en": "And then here for my counter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 230.37,
          "end": 233.37,
          "en": "that initialState simply is the number zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 233.37,
          "end": 236.19,
          "en": "But, and that's now really important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 236.19,
          "end": 240.72,
          "en": "when using NgRx, anything can be your State.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 240.72,
          "end": 243.42,
          "en": "It can be a number, as it's the case here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 243.42,
          "end": 245.31,
          "en": "It could also be some text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 245.31,
          "end": 247.98,
          "en": "It could be a Boolean value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 247.98,
          "end": 251.52,
          "en": "it could be an object with the counter value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 251.52,
          "end": 253.62,
          "en": "nested inside of it, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 253.62,
          "end": 256.56,
          "en": "And it could also be an array of course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 256.56,
          "end": 260.4,
          "en": "So whichever kind of data you need to manage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 260.4,
          "end": 263.187,
          "en": "In this case for this basic example here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 263.187,
          "end": 264.84,
          "en": "the counter is a number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 264.84,
          "end": 267.78,
          "en": "and therefore I'll just Store that number in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 267.78,
          "end": 270.12,
          "en": "But later in the section you'll also see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 270.12,
          "end": 273.15,
          "en": "more complex State examples.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 273.15,
          "end": 275.49,
          "en": "So here it's now this initialState value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 275.49,
          "end": 277.86,
          "en": "which I passed to createReducer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 277.86,
          "end": 279.96,
          "en": "and therefore of course I could have also just passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 279.96,
          "end": 281.25,
          "en": "zero in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 281.25,
          "end": 284.49,
          "en": "But it is a practice you will see quite a bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 284.49,
          "end": 287.97,
          "en": "that you define that initialState in a separate variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 287.97,
          "end": 291.18,
          "en": "or constant simply to make it a bit easier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 291.18,
          "end": 294,
          "en": "to quickly see what your initialState is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 294,
          "end": 296.76,
          "en": "if we take a look at this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 296.76,
          "end": 299.1,
          "en": "Of course, at the moment this file is pretty empty,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 299.1,
          "end": 302.73,
          "en": "but the more complex your State and your Reducer gets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 302.73,
          "end": 304.77,
          "en": "the more logic might be added here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 304.77,
          "end": 308.22,
          "en": "And being able to then quickly see the initialState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 308.22,
          "end": 310.8,
          "en": "can therefore be useful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 310.8,
          "end": 314.4,
          "en": "And with that, we now already actually got",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 314.4,
          "end": 317.79,
          "en": "everything we need to set up this Reducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 317.79,
          "end": 321.33,
          "en": "It's not too useful yet because it doesn't contain",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 321.33,
          "end": 323.58,
          "en": "any logic for changing that State,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 323.58,
          "end": 325.71,
          "en": "but it has an initialState,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 325.71,
          "end": 330.71,
          "en": "and therefore we can now connect this Reducer to this Store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 331.68,
          "end": 334.23,
          "en": "that's set up in the app module here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 334.23,
          "end": 336,
          "en": "in this module based app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 336,
          "end": 339.87,
          "en": "to make that data available in this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 339.87,
          "end": 342.54,
          "en": "And of course, I'll also show you how to do this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 342.54,
          "end": 345.15,
          "en": "in a standalone component app in a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 345.15,
          "end": 348.6,
          "en": "The Reducer code is always the same though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 348.6,
          "end": 351.51,
          "en": "So here we should then export this Reducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 351.51,
          "end": 354.45,
          "en": "to make it available outside of this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 354.45,
          "end": 358.83,
          "en": "And now, when using Ng modules, what you have to do is here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 358.83,
          "end": 361.23,
          "en": "in this Ng module based app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 361.23,
          "end": 364.89,
          "en": "in this place where the Store is in the end created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 364.89,
          "end": 367.59,
          "en": "with help of StoreModule.forRoot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 367.59,
          "end": 371.4,
          "en": "you should pass an object to forRoot.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 371.4,
          "end": 375.12,
          "en": "And then in that object you can pick any key of your choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 375.12,
          "end": 378.75,
          "en": "For example, counter to describe the kind of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 378.75,
          "end": 382.11,
          "en": "data piece you wanna add to that Store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 382.11,
          "end": 387.11,
          "en": "And then as a value for that key, you use your Reducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 387.48,
          "end": 390.51,
          "en": "In my case here, this counterReducer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 390.51,
          "end": 393.24,
          "en": "which of course the offer also must be imported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 393.24,
          "end": 396.42,
          "en": "And then it's used as a value for this key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 396.42,
          "end": 398.85,
          "en": "And if you had multiple Reducers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 398.85,
          "end": 401.43,
          "en": "for different parts of your application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 401.43,
          "end": 403.95,
          "en": "and different features of your application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 403.95,
          "end": 407.76,
